WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.195
This is EstateHub. A complete property marketplace front end, built with Next.js 16.

00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:13.835
Buyers search on a live map. Every pin is a price, and every filter is saved in the link, so a search can be shared.

00:00:14.335 --> 00:00:20.408
They open a listing, book a tour in a slot the seller has free, and reserve the home by bank transfer.

00:00:21.408 --> 00:00:28.313
From then on, the deal is tracked stage by stage. The buyer always knows what has been done and what comes next.

00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:33.201
They can compare homes side by side, and chat with the seller in real time.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:40.973
Sellers get their own portal. They add listings, handle tour requests, and see what each property has earned.

00:00:41.973 --> 00:00:44.398
Both portals come in light and in dark.

00:00:46.298 --> 00:00:59.539
Your team runs everything from the admin console. Approve listings one at a time, or a hundred in a batch. Verify identities. Work through each deal from a checklist. Confirm payments and send payouts.

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:06.886
Change the name, the logo and the brand colours from settings. No code, and no rebuild.

00:01:07.786 --> 00:01:09.550
And all of it works on a phone.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:23.491
Seventy-three finished pages, across the website, the buyer account, the seller portal and the admin console. Built on Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript and Tailwind.

00:01:24.791 --> 00:01:27.280
EstateHub. Start with it already built.
